      ],
      "consequence": "Severe yaw spin-out and loss of rotational heading hold.",
      "explanation": "Standard quadcopters counter-balance aerodynamic torque with 2 CW and 2 CCW motors. Reversing one motor makes three rotors spin clockwise and only one counter-clockwise, producing an inescapable 3:1 net yaw torque."
    }
